    { "id": "pick-a-direction", "x": 0, "y": -170, "w": 430, "text": "Direction vote, 2026-08-24: B — Art First won. Current work lives on the \"v3 — Paper\" page.", "page": "page-1" },
    { "id": "flow-modes", "x": 0, "y": -150, "w": 520, "text": "v1 flow — rejected as AI-looking (glass cards, blurred-art chrome). Kept for history.", "page": "page-2" },
    { "id": "v2-system", "x": 0, "y": -150, "w": 520, "text": "v2 — rejected as AI-looking (dark + glow + dot-matrix + grain). Kept for history.", "page": "page-3" },
    { "id": "v3-system", "x": 0, "y": -210, "w": 560, "text": "v3 — Paper. The brief from the Lovable prompt, executed: one warm paper ground, ink typography (Archivo), IBM Plex Mono only for machine values, hairline rules, flat surfaces, zero glow, zero grain, one signal-red accent used only for primary actions and alerts. The wall preview is the product photo: a black panel in a hairline frame, always in the same place. The only colour on screen is whatever the wall is showing. Mode/effect/preset strips are tappable.", "page": "page-4" },
    { "id": "v3-strip", "x": 530, "y": -130, "w": 460, "text": "Controls are one component: a hairline strip whose active cell inverts to ink. Sliders are tick rails with a flat round knob. No shadows anywhere on this page.", "page": "page-4" },
    { "id": "v3-journal", "x": 3810, "y": -130, "w": 460, "text": "Journal — PROPOSED feature, not in the app yet: the brain logs every push, the app shows what the wall has worn; tap a row to send it back. One of several feature candidates listed in chat.", "page": "page-4" }
  ],
